// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`lib/tap error registry > reads as one voice across every entry 1`] = `
"AMBIGUOUS_COMMAND
  That command id matches more than one row of the test.
  Qualify the id with the section it belongs to, as \`cypress tap reporter\` lists it.

ATTEMPT_NOT_FOUND
  That test has no such attempt.
  \`--attempt\` takes a 1-based attempt number and selects an earlier attempt of a retried test; omit it for the latest.

BINDING_NOT_FOUND
  Could not find the running Cypress in any open browser tab.
  The instance may still be loading, so try again in a moment. If the problem persists, the tab running Cypress may have been closed; open a browser in Cypress and try again.

BINDING_THREW
  The Cypress instance failed while running the command.
  Check the instance with \`cypress tap status\`, then try again.

CDP_UNREACHABLE
  Lost the debugging connection to the browser running Cypress.
  The browser may have just closed. Make sure Cypress is running with a browser open, then try again.

CLI_OUTDATED
  The running Cypress is newer than this CLI.
  Update the CLI with \`npm install --save-dev cypress@latest\`, then try again.

COMMAND_NOT_FOUND
  The test has no command matching that id.
  \`cypress tap reporter --test-id <id>\` lists this test’s commands and their ids.

FRAME_READ_FAILED
  Reading the app under test failed.
  The page may have navigated mid-read. Try again once it has settled.

GRAPHQL_FAILED
  The Cypress instance failed while answering a data query.
  Try the command again.

GRAPHQL_UNREACHABLE
  Could not reach the Cypress instance to read its data.
  The instance may have just closed. Make sure Cypress is running in open mode, then try again.

INSTANCE_OUTDATED
  The running Cypress is older than this CLI.
  Update Cypress in the running project with \`npm install --save-dev cypress@latest\`, restart it, then try again.

INVALID_ARGUMENTS
  The command was given an argument it cannot accept.
  Run \`cypress tap <command> --help\` for the arguments it takes.

INVALID_INDEX
  \`--at\` is not a valid index into the matched elements.
  \`--at\` takes a whole number, 0 or greater: a 0-based index into the elements \`--selector\` matched, so it needs a selector to index into and a match at that index.

INVALID_LIMIT
  A size limit was not a positive integer.
  Options that cap the size of a read — \`--max-chars\`, \`--max-nodes\` — take a positive integer.

INVALID_OPTIONS
  The command was given an option it cannot accept.
  Run \`cypress tap <command> --help\` for the options it takes.

INVALID_PAYLOAD
  The command was given input this CLI could not read.
  Run \`cypress tap <command> --help\` for the arguments and options it takes.

INVALID_SELECTOR
  The app under test rejected the selector as invalid CSS.
  Check the selector for a syntax error, such as an unclosed quote or bracket, then try again.

NO_AUT
  No app under test is loaded.
  Run a spec first with \`cypress tap run <spec>\`. To read the app as it was at an earlier command, pin that command with \`cypress tap pin\`.

NO_BROWSER_ATTACHED
  Cypress is running, but no test browser is open.
  Open a browser in Cypress, then try again.

NO_INSTANCE
  No running Cypress instance is available to drive.
  \`cypress tap\` drives a Cypress you already have open. Start one with \`cypress open\`, then try again.

NO_PROJECT
  The Cypress instance has no project open.
  Open a project in Cypress, then try again.

NO_RUN
  No spec has been run yet.
  Start one with \`cypress tap run <spec>\`, then read it once it has finished. \`cypress tap specs\` lists the specs this instance can run.

PIN_TARGET_REQUIRED
  The \`pin\` command was not told what to pin.
  Pass \`--test-id\` and \`--command-id\`, as listed by \`cypress tap reporter\`, or \`--clear\` to release the current pin.

PROTOCOL_MISMATCH
  The running Cypress answered in a way this CLI does not recognize.
  The running Cypress and this CLI are likely different versions. Update the older of the two with \`npm install --save-dev cypress@latest\`, then try again.

RENDERER_UNRESPONSIVE
  Cypress is reachable, but the page running it is not responding.
  It may be paused in DevTools, stuck in a loop, or starved of memory. Pass \`--timeout <ms>\` to wait longer.

RUN_FAILED
  The Cypress instance could not start the run.
  Check the instance with \`cypress tap status\`, then try again.

RUN_IN_PROGRESS
  A spec is currently running.
  Wait for it to finish — \`cypress tap status\` reports when it has — then try again.

SNAPSHOT_NOT_FOUND
  That command has no snapshot matching \`--at\`.
  \`--at\` takes a snapshot name or a 1-based index; omit it to pin the command’s final state.

SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE
  That command has no DOM snapshot to pin.
  Snapshots are captured in open mode and kept only for the most recent tests, as \`numTestsKeptInMemory\` sets. Run the spec again to capture fresh snapshots, or raise \`numTestsKeptInMemory\` to keep more.

SPEC_NOT_FOUND
  The instance has no spec matching that path.
  \`cypress tap specs\` lists the specs this instance can run. If the spec exists but is not listed, widen \`specPattern\` in the Cypress config.

STALE_HANDLE
  The Cypress instance navigated while running the command.
  Run the command again.

STALE_INSTANCE
  Cypress was running, but is no longer responding.
  It likely exited uncleanly. Start Cypress again with \`cypress open\`, then try again.

TEST_NOT_FOUND
  The run has no test matching that id.
  \`cypress tap reporter\` lists this run’s tests and their ids.

TESTING_TYPE_NOT_CONFIGURED
  That testing type is not configured for this project.
  Configure it in the Cypress config, or start Cypress in a testing type the project supports.

UNKNOWN_COMMAND
  That is not a command this Cypress offers.
  Run \`cypress tap --help\` to list the commands available."
`;
